WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.962
The most important danger is the first:
a failed read reported as a fix.

2
00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:08.194
An access error makes
yesterday's findings disappear,

3
00:00:08.194 --> 00:00:10.851
and without a guard
their issues would close.

4
00:00:10.851 --> 00:00:12.513
Here they stay unverified.

5
00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:16.941
The rest follow from the same habit
of not trusting what you can't prove:

6
00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:21.828
refuse runs that can't be compared, keep
secrets out entirely, pin every action,

7
00:00:21.828 --> 00:00:26.791
take the Graph host from the profile, keep
reading and writing in separate jobs,

8
00:00:26.791 --> 00:00:28.624
keep names out of the tracker,

9
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:32.880
and make the evidence unchangeable,
chained, and checked every day.
